X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10286
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10286
DTSTART:20261121T190000Z
DTEND:20261121T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261121T000000Z
SUMMARY:Winter Seed Sowing Workshop
DESCRIPTION:You don't have to wait until Spring to plan your garden -- in 
 fact\, Winter is the best time to start native seeds.\n\nNative plants are 
 a beautiful\, beneficial addition to any garden. And growing plants from 
 seed is an easy\, low cost way to add native plants to your landscaping. In 
 this free workshop\, using seeds from the Glen Ridge Native Seed Library\, 
 learn how to prepare your native seeds so they are ready to grow next 
 Spring. This process is called cold stratification\, which will be 
 explained with a how-to demonstration of the various methods you can use. 
 Choose from 90 New Jersey native species and get recommendations for your 
 yard based on growing conditions\, color\, and height. Learn how to grow 
 native plants with confidence and best practices for supporting wildlife in 
 your yard.\n\nSponsored by the Glen Ridge Environmental Advisory Committee.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10286-17822730
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17822730
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Libcal Bccls 10306": "https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15348446"}
X-SOURCE-ID:libcal_bccls_10306
X-SOURCE:Libcal Bccls 10306
DTSTART:20261121T190000Z
DTEND:20261121T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20261121T000000Z
SUMMARY:[Outside Org]  Aging in Montclair Saturday Social
DESCRIPTION:Program Title\n\nYankee Stadium: From the (Organ) Bench with Ed 
 Alstrom\n\nProgram Description\n\nJoin Aging in Montclair (AIM) for a 
 special behind-the-scenes look at Yankee Stadium with Ed Alstrom\, the New 
 York Yankees' longtime weekend organist.\n\nNow in his 23rd season at 
 Yankee Stadium\, Ed will share fascinating stories from the organ bench\, 
 demonstrate how he brings music to life during games\, and reveal how his 
 performances enhance the excitement and atmosphere of America's favorite 
 pastime.\n\nA graduate of Westminster Choir College\, Ed has enjoyed an 
 extraordinary musical career. He has performed with legendary artists 
 including Bette Midler\, Chuck Berry\, Leonard Bernstein\, Odetta\, and 
 Dion. He also served as associate conductor for Broadway's Hairspray\, 
 directed music Off-Broadway\, and released two acclaimed blues 
 albums.\n\nWhether you're a lifelong Yankees fan\, a baseball enthusiast\, 
 or simply curious about the music behind the game\, this engaging 
 presentation offers a unique perspective on one of baseball's most beloved 
 traditions.\n\n \n\nPresented by Aging in Montclair (AIM).
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Lectures / History & Culture, Meeting, Music, Outside Organization, Personal Growth
UID:LibCal-10306-15348446
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15348446
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairlocal": "https://montclairlocal.news/event/candlelight-breathwork-with-julie-billy/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairlocal
X-SOURCE:Montclair Local News
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261121T210000
DTSTAMP:20261113T153301Z
CREATED:20261113T153301Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261113T153301Z
UID:10143345-1795287600-1795294800@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:Candlelight Breathwork with Julie & Billy
DESCRIPTION:An immersive evening of breath\, connection\, and renewal. \nFor one special evening\, Loopwell transforms into an intimate\, candlelit sanctuary for a guided breathwork experience with Julie and Billy of Spirit 11ouse. \nSurrounded by soft candlelight\, lush greenery\, and a calming atmosphere\, you’ll be invited to slow down\, turn inward\, and reconnect with yourself through the power of breath. \nBreathwork is an accessible practice that can support self-awareness\, relaxation\, and a deeper connection between mind and body. Julie and Billy will introduce the therapeutic benefits of breathwork for self-care and well-being\, then guide you step by step through a three-part active breathing technique in a safe\, supportive environment. \nWhether you’re new to breathwork or looking to deepen your practice\, this experience offers dedicated time to pause\, explore\, and recharge. \nYour experience includes: \nAn introduction to the benefits of breathwork for self-care and well-being \nStep-by-step guidance through a three-part active breathing technique \nA candlelit setting surrounded by greenery and calming sensory elements \nA safe\, supportive space to reconnect with yourself and your breath \nMake yourself comfortable: We recommend bringing a blanket\, eye mask\, and water. A yoga mat is also welcome to help you settle in. \nJulie and Billy from Spirit 11ouse leading a breathwork session at Loopwell in Montclair\nAbout Julie and Billy\nBreathwork instructors Billy and Julie co-created Spirit 11ouse\, to forever stay connected to a path of healing\, expansion\, and connection. Billy and Julie like to see themselves as a bridge between you and ancient practices that will ultimately bring you home to yourself\, others\, and Spirit. Billy had a private practice as a licensed psychotherapist for 15 years and has directed nearly 60 mindfulness retreats with local high school students. In addition\, Billy is also a certified yoga instructor. Julie brings nearly 25 years of entrepreneurship to their venture and is passionate about impacting the lives of others. She is the founder of Chavez for Charity which proudly donated $1.6 million to different charitable organizations worldwide. Both are passionate about making the people they work with feel at home and supported. \nBeyond their dedication to guiding and serving others\, they cherish time with their four kids and all the adventure that family life brings. \nLearn more: spirit11ouse.com\nInstagram: @spirit11ouse \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/candlelight-breathwork-with-julie-billy/
LOCATION:Loopwell\, 80 Maple Ave\, Montclair\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://montclairlocal.news/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Candle-Light-Wellness-Room.jpeg
END:VEVENT
