DTSTAMP:20261201T000000Z
SUMMARY:Spend the Holidays in The Twilight Zone
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. \n\nRod Serling wrote a few 
 stories for The Twilight Zone about the holiday spirit and\nspecifically\, 
 about Christmas. Born on December 25th in 1924\, Rod was known to 
 often\nsay\, ”I came as a present unwrapped.” Though Rod was Jewish\, 
 he and his family\nenjoyed celebrating Christmas among friends and 
 neighbors in his hometown of\nBinghamton\, NY.\n\n\nTwo of his wonderfully 
 creative holiday episodes will be presented and discussed in the\nupcoming 
 micro-marathon.\n\n\nThe first is entitled\, “The Night of the Meek”: 
 S2:E11\nA downtrodden\, drunken department store Santa angers his employers 
 and is fired from\nhis job. He wanders aimlessly in the streets of the city 
 until he finds a magic sack that is\nfilled with gifts that can fulfill 
 everyone’s wish\, including his. Art Carney is stellar as the\nSanta 
 Claus that finds his “True North”.\n\nThe second is entitled\, “Five 
 Characters in Search of an Exit”: S3:E14\nThe title tells the story. An 
 ensemble cast of characters in a very strange\, nondescript\nplace don’t 
 who they are\, where they are and why they are there. What they need is 
 to\ndetermine how they can escape their surroundings. When they reach the 
 exit\, all\nquestions are answered.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-17711100
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17711100
END:VEVENT
