SUMMARY:Book Talk: 20 Over 60 by Beth Weinhouse and David Galef
DESCRIPTION:In their new anthology 20 OVER 60 (Regal House\; October 6\, 
 2026)\, editors Beth Weinhouse and David Galef—also co-editors of 
 the\nanthology 20 OVER 40—present a portrait of later life that is 
 consistently overlooked\, in a culture obsessed with youth. The twenty 
 short stories—including ones by Joyce Carol Oates\, Paul Theroux\, and 
 Jane Gardam—are vibrant\, moving\, and often hilarious\, capturing the 
 texture of life after sixty in all its complexity.\n\nAmong the characters 
 readers will meet: a retired couple whose hobby is stealing pepper mills 
 from high-end restaurants\, a woman juggling her husband and ex-husband 
 staying in the same hospital\, a futuristic nursing home whose designers 
 become its unhappy residents\, an older woman trying her hand at online 
 dating\, and a grandfather helping his granddaughter scatter her mother's 
 ashes. These smart and poignant stories make the case that the years after 
 sixty are as strange\, surprising\, and vivid as the decades that came 
 before—and that readers living it deserve to see themselves on the 
 page.\n\nIn an early review\, Library Journal called 20 OVER 60 
 "remarkable\," adding\, "The editors succeed in creating an outstanding 
 anthology that emphasizes that life continues to have vibrancy and 
 significance after 60."\n\nAbout the Co-Editors\nBeth Weinhouse has been an 
 editor at many mainstream magazines\, including Self\, Parenting\, 
 Prevention\, Redbook\, and Reader's Digest. She' s written feature articles 
 and book reviews for New York Newsday\, the Los Angeles Times Magazine\, 
 Travel & Leisure\, Town & Country\, Columbia Magazine\, and more. Her first 
 book was The Healthy Traveler\, about maintaining health away from home. 
 Her second book\, co-written with Leslie Laurence\, was Outrageous 
 Practices\, about how gender bias can threaten women's health. More at 
 bethweinhouse.com.\n\nDavid Galef has published over a dozen books\, 
 including the novel Flesh\, the short story collection My Date with 
 Neanderthal Woman\, the children' s book Tracks\, Japanese Proverbs: Wit 
 and Wisdom\, and Brevity: A Flash Fiction Handbook. Day job: English 
 professor and creative writing program director at Montclair State 
 University. He's also the editor of Vestal Review\, the longest-running 
 flash fiction magazine on the planet. Find him at davidgalef.com.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Talk
UID:LibCal-10306-17387649
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17387649
END:VEVENT
