SUMMARY:Everything Book Club\, "Life & Death & Giants" by Ron Rindo
DESCRIPTION:\n\nAn American tall tale with a surprising plot and the heart 
 of a giant. Gabriel Fisher is born an orphan\, weighing 18 pounds and 
 measuring 27 inches long. Gabriel gets taken in by his devout Amish 
 grandparents who try to protect him from the "English" world. But it’s 
 hard to hide when you’re nearly 8 feet tall. When Gabriel reaches 17\, 
 the local football coach spots him tossing hay bales like sofa cushions. 
 What happens next transforms not only Gabriel’s life but the lives of 
 everyone he meets. \n\n\n\n"'Life\, and Death\, and Giants' is an 
 intriguing and alluring novel from beginning to end....Reading it is like 
 meeting a family that you never knew existed and becoming close friends in 
 a few weeks. Highly recommended." --Jane Smiley\n\n\n\nRON RINDO is a 
 professor of English and creative writing at the University of 
 Wisconsin-Oshkosh. He has published one previous novel\, "Breathing Lake 
 Superior\, "and three short story collections. He lives in Pickett\, 
 Wisconsin.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Teen Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-16721233
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16721233
END:VEVENT
